WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.680
Let me ask you to back up just a little bit and tell me about the work you did as a county extension agent.

2
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:09.120
What did that involve?

3
00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.680
Well, today of course, it’s much different.

4
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:27.000
In that day, it was the beginning . . . the Extension Act was passed in Congress in 1914 and by the time I got into it in 1920,

5
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:32.000
1919, 1920, they hadn’t done much groundwork.

6
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:46.760
So the county agent didn’t have much of a . . . But it was a day and time when there was a lot of anthrax in cattle and horses and the disease known commonly as charbon.

7
00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:50.820
And there was a tremendous amount of hog cholera all over the state.

8
00:00:50.820 --> 00:01:00.420
So I spent most of my time vaccinating hogs for hog cholera and vaccinating cattle and horses and mules for anthrax.

9
00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:16.960
So, but then St. John Plantation is a ten-thousand-acre sugarcane farm in St. Martin Parish and they had never used fertilizer.

10
00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:22.000
Nobody in St. Martin Parish had ever used fertilizer in their work.

11
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:30.240
So I brought test plots for the first time in the parish using fertilizer and that was back in 1921.

12
00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:39.260
So that . . . Were the results impressive?

13
00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:39.687
Did they . . .

14
00:01:39.687 --> 00:01:42.980
Oh, the results were very, very impressive.

15
00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:53.160
They soon saw how much of an increased tonnage there was in the fertilized plot that it became standard practice with them.

16
00:01:53.160 --> 00:02:00.700
But the common ordinary farmer, who had very little education if any,

17
00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:09.040
they couldn’t see the value of spending hard money in June to get better results in December.

18
00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:10.220
They couldn’t see that far.

19
00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:10.420
I see.

20
00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:16.280
So it took a long time to get the fertilizer idea over in the farmers.

21
00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:20.380
But that was the main work that county agents did in the early days.
